  "query_preview": "period as well. \n\nA weak shortwave passage through central IL has been trending later \nin the week over the last few forecast cycles. Now it looks to pass \nthrough on Thursday, possibly bringing some light sprinkles near and \nnorth of the IL River Valley. However, it could pass without any \nactivity due to how dry our airmass is. \n\nThe next best chance for any rain is more likely to arrive this next \nweekend, just in time for Halloween festivities. A stronger \nshortwave appears to pulse through IL Saturday/Sunday next week, \nbringing a 40-60% chance for showers. Amounts are forecast to be \npretty minimal, but there is time for this forecast to change. \nTiming/location/amounts will continue to shift as we move \ncloser. Trends will continue to be monitored with future \nforecasts.",
